(1713863, 229838, 35804, '<td valign="top">..."natural"?...an elegant image indeed, but I am a little hard pressed to see "natural" in this image...the lovely "posed" , or at least camera aware model is wearing quite a bit of makeup, the calla lily...not sure if it''s real...and this appears to be an image made in a studio type of setting? I could be dreadfully wrong...and I do apologise ahead of time if I am...but for me, and I have been ripped for "title" comments before... the title, border, and image are a package deal...if they don''t matter as some say...why add them.</td>', '..."natural"?...an elegant image indeed, but I am a little hard pressed to see "natural" in this image...the lovely "posed" , or at least camera aware model is wearing quite a bit of makeup, the calla lily...not sure if it''s real...and this appears to be an image made in a studio type of setting? I could be dreadfully wrong...and I do apologise ahead of time if I am...but for me, and I have been ripped for "title" comments before... the title, border, and image are a package deal...if they don''t matter as some say...why add them.', '2005-09-16 11:32:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1713867, 229673, 39664, '<td valign="top">What a beautiful portrait!  I love her peaches and cream complexion with the freckles.  She may one day hate them then learn to celebrate them.  Only thing, I wish her eyes were less shadowed so they would pop against the red hair. 8</td>', 'What a beautiful portrait!  I love her peaches and cream complexion with the freckles.  She may one day hate them then learn to celebrate them.  Only thing, I wish her eyes were less shadowed so they would pop against the red hair. 8', '2005-09-16 11:35:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1713872, 230367, 39664, '<td valign="top">Too many shadows and the necklace is a distraction to me.  IMHO, limit distractions such as jewelry and props because a portrait should bring the viewer''s focus to the subject, not the clasp of the necklace or shadows.  I also like to see the eyes facing the same direction as the face.  Hope this helps!</td>', 'Too many shadows and the necklace is a distraction to me.  IMHO, limit distractions such as jewelry and props because a portrait should bring the viewer''s focus to the subject, not the clasp of the necklace or shadows.  I also like to see the eyes facing the same direction as the face.  Hope this helps!', '2005-09-16 11:38:53.000000', NULL, 1),
