(1745595, 229508, 13026, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Joey Lawrence:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by christie3:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by art-inept:</b></div><hr/><i> hah christie, very joey-esque. people might dock you for the detail-less hair though. did you use curves? because it''s hard to control certain areas in curves as some highlights will be blown out and some dark spots will lose all detail. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Lol Justin...very Joey?  I wish!  :P<br/>:) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Needs more dirt. :-D </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Lol.  :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Joey Lawrence: Originally posted by christie3: Originally posted by art-inept: hah christie, very joey-esque. people might dock you for the detail-less hair though. did you use curves? because it''s hard to control certain areas in curves as some highlights will be blown out and some dark spots will lose all detail.  Lol Justin...very Joey?  I wish!  :P:)  Needs more dirt. :-D  Lol.  :)', '2005-09-28 13:59:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1746966, 228826, 12243, '<td valign="top">i think this photo is really sweet. I love the glow. Take it from me who also HATES her photo being taken. I''m glad she likes this one. It is lovely.</td>', 'i think this photo is really sweet. I love the glow. Take it from me who also HATES her photo being taken. I''m glad she likes this one. It is lovely.', '2005-09-28 22:52:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1747402, 228978, 35218, '<td valign="top">Overprocessed or not?<br/> <br/>I think the processing done here lifts this image above the crowd.  It''s not just ''another portrait''.  It creates a very unusual effect - a plastic ''baby doll'' look as has been mentioned.  I think this is ''overprocessed'' even for the front page of a glamour magazine.  I would put this as much more of a personal artistic endeavour which pushes the envelope to create something that is on the border between beautiful and disturbing. <br/> <br/>The only issue I would raise is the fringing around the nose and lips from sharpening.<br/> <br/>Other than that - well done Katherine.  Do some more.</td>', 'Overprocessed or not? I think the processing done here lifts this image above the crowd.  It''s not just ''another portrait''.  It creates a very unusual effect - a plastic ''baby doll'' look as has been mentioned.  I think this is ''overprocessed'' even for the front page of a glamour magazine.  I would put this as much more of a personal artistic endeavour which pushes the envelope to create something that is on the border between beautiful and disturbing.  The only issue I would raise is the fringing around the nose and lips from sharpening. Other than that - well done Katherine.  Do some more.', '2005-09-29 02:28:59.000000', NULL, 0),
